30,2,,status,Sakura,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
31,2,,status,Servas,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Misaki,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,May,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Kenji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,May,,"It's worse than I thought. Two people use the room almost exclusively, and the fridge was a graveyard of abandoned food.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"The wall is basically paper. I can hear every word of a phone call. Plus, we're all eating at our desks now.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Servas,,A hot lunch takes twenty-five minutes round trip. That is a significant waste of our limited vitality.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Sakura,,"We spent 68,000 yen last year on outside rentals for tiny groups! We are literally paying to leave the building.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"We're strangers. The only ""social"" spot is the printer, and the last serious talk happened in front of everyone.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,May,,"@Sakura, if we're paying for outside rooms, why not just fix this one? But we need a system for the cleaning.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"If we make it a kitchen, the crumbs at the desks might stop, but the noise will just change type.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Servas,,A kitchen would save those twenty-five minutes. That's hours of life reclaimed every week for the whole office.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Sakura,,"The quotes are 141,000 for a meeting setup and 96,000 for a kitchen. The kitchen is cheaper and stops the rental fees.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"A kitchen is social, but it's not private. We still have no place for the ""awkward"" but necessary conversations.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,May,,"@Kenji, a meeting space would be bookable. That solves the ""first come, first served"" chaos I hate.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Misaki,,A quiet room would solve my noise problem entirely. No more eavesdropping on phone calls through the plasterboard.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Servas,,But a quiet room doesn't solve the lunch trek. We must consider the physical toll of our daily routines.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Sakura,,"From a budget view, the meeting space is the most expensive, but it replaces those 68,000 yen rental invoices.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"If we just make it a quiet room, we're still strangers who can't talk. We need a functional social or professional hub.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,May,,"We have to choose between eating, meeting, or silence.","{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"Silence sounds like heaven, but I see the point about the desks being messy.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Servas,,I lean toward the kitchen. Health and time are the most precious resources we have.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Sakura,,I'm weighing the rental savings against the fit-out costs. A meeting space pays for itself faster.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Kenji,,I just want us to stop having difficult conversations in the middle of the open office.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,,status,Sakura,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
56,3,,status,Servas,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
57,3,,status,Misaki,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
58,3,,status,May,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
59,3,,status,Kenji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,May,,"Let's look at the options. A kitchen is great for health, but a meeting space is the only one with a calendar.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Misaki,,A quiet room is the only one that actually protects the people sitting next to the wall from the noise.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Servas,,The open kitchen promotes wellness. It removes the stress of the daily commute for food.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Sakura,,The meeting space is the most professional. It stops the leakage of funds to outside hire.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"A meeting space allows for those private, necessary talks that we are currently avoiding or doing publicly.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,May,,"@Sakura, if we go with the meeting space, can we ensure the booking system is strictly enforced?","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Misaki,,I'm worried a meeting space is just more talking. A quiet room is a sanctuary.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Servas,,"A sanctuary is fine, but a hungry worker is an inefficient worker. The kitchen is the most vital.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Sakura,,The financial logic is strong for the meeting space. It's an investment that stops a recurring loss.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Misaki, we can find silence elsewhere, but we can't find a private room for a heart-to-heart in this office.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,May,,"I'm torn, but the fairness of a booking calendar wins for me. No more fighting for the room.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"I still prefer the quiet room, but if everyone wants to talk or eat, I'll concede to the most useful.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Servas,,I cannot ignore the twenty-five minute walk. I vote for the kitchen for the sake of our energy.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Sakura,,I'm voting for the meeting space. The numbers don't lie; we need a professional area.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"I agree with Sakura. We need a place to actually be a team, even if it's for difficult talks.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,May,,I'm set on the meeting space.,"{""words"":6,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Misaki,,I'll vote for the quiet room. I can't handle the noise anymore.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Servas,,I stay with the kitchen.,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Sakura,,Meeting space.,"{""words"":2,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Kenji,,Meeting space.,"{""words"":2,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
